am; adding them helps prevent alias-driven duplicate rows and missed PubMed retrievals.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68010889"]},{"current_value":"No for epilepsy indication","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"No FDA-approved epilepsy indication; no current FDA/openFDA label, Drugs@FDA record, or NDC listing found for piracetam/Nootropil.","rationale":"FDA/openFDA label, Drugs@FDA, and NDC API searches returned no matches. Drugs@FDA covers most FDA-approved drug products since 1939, and the NDC endpoint covers final marketed drug listings submitted to FDA.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=piracetam&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=piracetam&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/ndc.json?search=generic_name:%22PIRACETAM%22&limit=1","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database","https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/ndc/"]},{"current_value":"Not FDA-cleared for epilepsy or not marketed in U.S.","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Not FDA-approved for epilepsy; no current FDA/openFDA label, Drugs@FDA record, or NDC listing found for piracetam/Nootropil.","rationale":"Drug products are FDA-approved, not FDA-cleared. FDA/openFDA and Drugs@FDA/NDC searches support no current FDA approval/marketing record found for these terms.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=piracetam&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/ndc.json?search=generic_name:%22PIRACETAM%22&limit=1","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Cortical myoclonus; Myoclonic","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Cortical myoclonus; Myoclonic","rationale":"UK SmPC indicates Nootropil for myoclonus of cortical origin; ILAE lists piracetam among treatment options for progressive myoclonic epilepsies.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/smpc","https://www.ilae.org/index.cfm?objectid=6C4D71BD-EE34-B816-27EB767D97DE334A"]},{"current_value":"Tablet/capsule; oral solution; injection in some markets","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Film-coated tablets; oral solution; solution for injection/infusion in some EU markets","rationale":"UK eMC verifies 800/1200 mg film-coated tablets and 33% oral solution. EMA nationally authorised product list verifies injection/infusion products in some EU member states. Capsule is not supported by the reviewed trusted sources.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/ingredient/813","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101132/smpc","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/psusa/piracetam-list-nationally-authorised-medicinal-products-psusa00002429202204_en.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; IV/IM injection; Liquid; Tablet","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Injection/infusion solution; Liquid/oral solution; Tablet","rationale":"Trusted sources support oral solution, film-coated tablets, and injection/infusion products, but not capsule or specifically IV/IM route wording.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/ingredient/813","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/psusa/piracetam-list-nationally-authorised-medicinal-products-psusa00002429202204_en.pdf"]},{"current_value":"4-5 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Approximately 5 h (plasma half-life in young adult men)","rationale":"The UK SmPC states plasma half-life is 5.0 hours in young adult men; the 4 h lower bound was not supported by reviewed trusted sources.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101132/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Minimal metabolism; renal excretion","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"No metabolite found; excreted almost completely in urine, with clearance dependent on renal creatinine clearance","rationale":"SmPC supports no known metabolite and predominantly urinary elimination; the proposed text is more precise.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101132/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Not a CYP inducer/inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"No clinically meaningful CYP inhibition expected; metabolic interaction with other drugs is unlikely","rationale":"SmPC supports low interaction potential and no inhibition of major CYP isoforms at tested concentrations, with only minor high-concentration CYP2A6/CYP3A4/5 effects. It does not directly prove absence of CYP induction.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101132/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Mode of action in cortical myoclonus is unknown; do not classify as a direct GABAergic ASM despite being a cyclic GABA derivative.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Mode of action in cortical myoclonus is unknown; do not classify as a direct GABAergic ASM despite being a GABA analogue.","rationale":"SmPC states the mode of action in cortical myoclonus is unknown; eMC PIL calls Nootropil a GABA analogue. The row's caution against direct GABAergic classification is appropriate.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/smpc","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/pil"]},{"current_value":"GABA","field":"filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"Unknown/Other","rationale":"The SmPC says piracetam's mode of action in cortical myoclonus is unknown. A GABA filter implies a direct GABAergic mechanism that the row itself warns against.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Limited","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Limited","rationale":"Limited confidence is supported because the SmPC says the mode of action is unknown.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/smpc"]},{"current_value":"UK eMC SmPC labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"UK eMC SmPC labeling","rationale":"The mechanism statement is directly supported by UK eMC SmPC text.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/smpc"]},{"current_value":"EMA/UK SmPC","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"UK SmPC","rationale":"The cited mechanism source is UK eMC SmPC. EMA product-list evidence supports formulations but is not the mechanism source.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101131/smpc"]},{"current_value":"CNS: hyperkinesia 1.7%, metabolic: weight gain 1.3%, psychiatric: nervousness 1.1%, CNS: somnolence 0.9%, GI: diarrhea 0.8%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: hyperkinesia (common); CNS: somnolence (uncommon); psychiatric: nervousness (common); weight increased (common, investigations); GI: diarrhea/diarrhoea (frequency not known)","rationale":"Current trusted SmPC supports adverse reaction frequency categories, not the exact percentages. It lists diarrhea/diarrhoea as frequency not known, which conflicts with an exact 0.8% value.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/101132/smpc"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect es